error[ffi_constant_type]: `B_SEVEN` in `fixedbugs-2075-unevaluated.h` cannot be declared `i32`: clang refuses the header's value at line 4: its expression holds an operation C leaves undefined for the operands it is given, and the program's own unit, built with clang's checks for an overflow, a shift, a division by zero and a float out of an integer's range, traps where it reads it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2075-an-undefined-operation-in-builtin-constant-p-is-refused.hero:11:5
     |
  11 |     constant B_SEVEN: i32  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2075-unevaluated.h` line 4 reads `#define B_SEVEN (__builtin_constant_p(2147483647 + unevaluated_one) ? 7 : 7)`
  note: an operation C leaves undefined gives no value: wherever C computes it, a program reading `B_SEVEN` reads whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines
